 "scope": "Federer 4.1.26, pp. 383-384: for a Lipschitzian f from R^m to R^m and a bounded Lebesgue measurable set A, the signed degree (degree f|A)(y), the exact signed numerical sum of sign det Df over the fibre A intersect f^{-1}{y}, exists for Lebesgue almost all y; f_#(E^m restricted to A) = E^m restricted to (degree f|A); the degree is Lebesgue almost constant on each component of R^m minus f(Bdry A); for connected A with f(A) disjoint from f(Bdry A) it is almost constant on f(A); and, if f|A is univalent, sign det Df is almost constant on A intersect {J_m f > 0}. Every dimension, including R^0, is retained.",
